Package: causatr
Title: Unified Causal Effect Estimation for Methodological Triangulation
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Lorenzo", "Fabbri", , "lorenzo.fabbri92sm@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-3031-322X"))
Description: Estimates causal effects via g-computation, inverse probability
    weighting (IPW), augmented IPW (doubly-robust), and matching for
    methodological triangulation. Primary engine is the parametric g-formula
    and iterated conditional expectation (ICE) g-computation with empirical
    sandwich variance estimation. Ships a self-contained density-ratio IPW
    engine, a doubly-robust AIPW estimator, and delegates matching to
    MatchIt. Supports binary, continuous, categorical, and multivariate
    treatments; static, dynamic, modified treatment, and stochastic
    interventions (stochastic is g-computation only); continuous, binary,
    count (Poisson, negative binomial), quasibinomial (fractional), Gamma,
    and beta regression outcomes; and external observation weights.
    Longitudinal data is handled via ICE g-computation, longitudinal IPW,
    and longitudinal AIPW. Transportability and generalizability via
    sampling-odds reweighting with a target population indicator.
    Cluster-robust sandwich variance is supported via the cluster argument.
